Z||000000||Raydar||02-06-2001||01:03 PM||||Neither our local phone company or cable company has seen fit to provide my area with any kind of broadband service. I am exploring alternatives. <BR>It appears that DirecPC is now offering satellite downloads only, with a phone-line upload, while Starband (DISH network) is offering satellite download as well as uplink. Download speeds for both systems seem to be in the range of 400-500K.<BR>I am familiar with the shortcomings of satellite regarding rain-fade and such, but that's about it. Has anyone here had experience with DirecPC or Starband? Or any other satellite broadband providers?<P>Thanks!  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||02-06-2001||05:12 PM||||Starband is only making something like 5000 units nationwide for the first year, so expect to be on a waitiing list and pay alot for it. A friend of mine uses DirectPC, it works great if you just want to web surf or download things, but you have a lot of lag time if you want to play games (like up to 5 second ping times) because of the fact that you have to send a comand through the phone line to your isp then to the DirectPC server then have them send it back to you. But you probably already knew that.||||reg||1
